 "poem": "But I am our Lord, although\nWe are not to hear him also;\nAnd he had found us and saw away\nOur manhood in our hands array,\nWhilst the light of his salvation\nWas darkening up against,\nAs they were making the right way away.\nNow he had made his choice as against\nThe castle from which we withdrew\nFor many a year: when into\nAn open field, through the grasses array,\nHe cried out to us all for flight: away",
